 ### Detail Coefficient Representation
-This variant reduces memory to 4 bytes per voxel by distributing bits over X, Y, Z as 12+10+10, supporting volumes up to $4096 \times 1024 \times 1024$ [S2]. Coordinates are packed into two `GL_SHORT` values. Unpacking is performed in a vertex program. For GPUs lacking bit shift/logical operators, unpacking is emulated with multiplication by a fraction (using `floor` Cg-function) and subtraction [S2]. This adds computation but is outweighed by memory savings and improved memory bandwidth to voxel count ratio [S2].
